+# Final report — 2026-10-10-glm-prefill-250-vllm
+
+**Objective:** Port the weight-stationary prefill execution model proven by davidcanar/vllm-strix-halo (278-294 tok/s GLM-5.3-Flash prefill on the same 2x Strix Halo TP=2 pair over Thunderbolt) into gufo's glm5_next kernel families, reaching >= 250 tok/s serving-level (HTTP through the pair) prefill while preserving the correctness contracts: chunked-vs-tokenwise byte identity, CPU-oracle RMS caps, cross-rank hash equality, and double-precision indexer top-k. The F32-family double-accumulation contract may be relaxed to float accumulation ONLY with measured evidence it is the binding constraint, both kernel twins switched together, re-derived/verified oracle caps, and reviewer signoff; no other contract is relaxable.
+
+**Verdict:** PASS
+
+| Phase | Status | Commit | Unresolved |
+| ----- | ------ | ------ | ---------- |
+| 1. vLLM review + weights-once attack plan | done | 485ad018 | 0 |
+| 2. Expert grouped-GEMM weight-stationary rewrite | done | a706c4bf | 0 |
+| 3. Q8_0 QuantTiled weight-stationary GEMM | done | 15660161 | 0 |
+| 4. F32 tiled family weight-stationary (double accumulation default) | done | 766bc3b6 | 0 |
+| 5. Pair: chunk-width re-sweep + exchange accounting | done | b0b439a7 | 1 |
+| 6. Package + serving qualification | done | b306c8eb | 0 |
+| 7. Residual iteration + final verify/docs | done | 84e53a29 | 0 |
+
+## Reviewer findings
+
+(none — clean sweep)
+
+## Phase handoffs
+
+- Phase 1 (vLLM review + weights-once attack plan): Phase 1 (vLLM review + weights-once attack plan) done with no functional source changes. Built gpu-test (602/602 + gate targets), studied /root/vllm-strix-halo read-only (README, PATCHES §6/§8/§42/§44, vsh_moe_int4.hip, moe-configs, vsh_w8a16, vsh_bench/vsh_ab), reproduced the slice baseline at 832.8 tok/s (the ~835 band, at 512 tokens — documented that tok/s falls to 713.7 at 4096 tokens from depth-dependent MLA/indexer families), re-ran all slice gates (8/8 PASS, executor oracle 7.484e-07 bit-identical to prior phases), re-measured DRAM read 240.24 GB/s, corrected the per-rank expert table to 87.65 GB via direct GGUF census (final-250.md understated it 2x), and wrote notes/vllm-250.md with their methodology, the weights-once roofline at 1024/2048/4096 x 100/50/35% of ceiling plus the 2.27 ms/token serial term, per-family efficiency targets for 250 and ~290 tok/s, ported and rejected technique lists mapped to gufo kernel families, and a 5-step quantified attack order. Committed 485ad01; production active, /ready 200 at phase end.
+- Phase 2 (Expert grouped-GEMM weight-stationary rewrite): Fix round complete. Landed the phase deliverable: BatchExpertGroupedWsKernel<Bucket,StageB,Warps,Rows> (the A-family weight-stationary template, Sub16+Vec only) in kernels_batch.hip.cpp with a three-regime launcher dispatch in BatchExpertQ8KGrouped — prefill n≥64 runs <32,16,32,1> (82 VGPRs/16 waves, weight re-read ⌈bucket/32⌉≈1.13× vs the generic tile's ≈2×), decode n<64 runs <16,8,16,2> (17.5 KiB LDS, n=1 launches 25-40% faster), and Q8_0/odd geometry keeps the original generic kernel verbatim; grid math and the executor are untouched, and prof.py's stage map gained the new kernel name. Fixed the two bench harness bugs the reviewers found (tokenwise loop now scatters global pair indices; full-N routing re-run before every chunked launch), retracted the false 'latent V0 anomaly' — V0 and all variants are chunked-vs-tokenwise identical in 160/160 checks at N∈{96,128,384,513,1024}×4 shapes×2 routings, re-verified on an -O2 rebuild matching production codegen. Ran the full gate suite on the integrated tree: executor oracle PASS at the unchanged 7.484e-07 (bit-identical twins), exec-513 ×3 / exec-2052 / exec-2049 byte-identical (exercising cross-regime dispatch), dsa_ops/batch_select/kda/mhc PASS, decode guard 16.60 ms/token (inside 16.6-16.9), check-format PASS 557 files. Measured before/after with matched binaries on a quiet GPU (production parked for the A/B after the probe OOM-killed it, then restored): slice 834.1-836.5→841.0 tok/s @512 and 713.7→716.2 @4096; pair probe 87.9/86.4→89.2/88.9 tok/s (disjoint bands, +2.2%); expert family per 512-chunk 81.6→78.8 ms (rocprofv3, Ws kernel confirmed dispatching). Wrote notes/experts-ws-250.md with the full variant sweep table (shapes, VGPR/waves, LDS, timings, bit-identity), the rejected Y-family, the winner + dispatch, the re-read-factor roofline table (1.13 ≤ 2), the explicit unit interpretation of the 3479 ms mandate, and the measured blocking-ceiling derivation: the family is register/occupancy-bound (same-traffic VGPR pairs separate 40%; 2× x-mandate costs only +9%; every rpb-raising shape spills or loses occupancy), the x-restaging term (4.3 GB/call at 1024-wide TP2 gate vs 0.68 GB weights-once) is register-capped, and the 3.86× cut is unreachable by tile restructuring within {256 VGPR, 64 KiB LDS, twin bit-identity} — the ceiling branch of criterion 1.
+- Phase 3 (Q8_0 QuantTiled weight-stationary GEMM): Built tools/bench/quant_ws_bench.hip (V0 verbatim copy plus three weight-stationary restructure families: W global-x wide tiles, L LDS group re-staging, Z XOR-swizzled unpadded LDS at exactly 64 KiB) and swept them against the landed BatchQuantTiledKernel on the seven real GLM shapes at n∈{96,513,1024,2048}+small-n, all bit-identical to V0 including the V0(n=1)×N executor-twin pattern. Every restructure measured 1.2-2× slower; the winner is the landed T16/rpb64 kernel, so no production kernel change lands. The mandate itself is at the hardware ceiling: the traffic model (weights n/T + x-restaging (m/rpb)·n·k·4, validated standalone 212-241 GB/s, slice in-situ 198 GB/s, pair 236 GB/s) shows the family's 4300 ms/2048 is its 509 GB/chunk stream at ~99% of the 240.24 GB/s peak — the brief's '51%' divided only the 262 GB weight term, ignoring the equal-magnitude x-restaging term — and ≤1500 ms needs ≥340 GB/s, unreachable even at zero weight re-read (weights-once+x floors at 2090 ms/2048). All gates re-ran green on the final tree (oracle 7.484e-07 identical, 513×3/2052/2049 byte-identical, kda/dsa/mhc/batch_select PASS, decode guard 16.56 ms/token, check-format PASS); production /ready=200 throughout. A mid-phase harness bug (variant token-width switch fallthrough → grid overshoot → unsigned wrap) that had produced inflated L/Z times and bogus 'stack faults' was found, fixed, retracted in the note, and all conclusions re-verified on the corrected run.
+- Phase 4 (F32 tiled family weight-stationary (double accumulation default)): Ported the weight-stationary execution model into the F32 dense-projection family (BatchF32TiledKernel -> templated BatchF32WsKernel) and, with the full pre-approved evidence chain, switched the family's accumulation from double to float: measured on-chip f64 FMA ceiling 461.5 GFLOP/s vs 8385 fp32 makes even a perfect double kernel floor at 2560 ms/2048 tokens (above the 2200 mandate), and bit-identical weight-stationary DOUBLE variants cutting traffic 2-4x measured 0.97-1.02x (family f64-pipe-bound, not traffic-bound; rocprof HW counters don't collect on this stack, so the chain is peak microbench + FLOP arithmetic + traffic controls + ISA mix, all documented). Winner tile T32/K512/W32/R2 float (64 KiB LDS, n/32 weight re-read) for n>=128, T8/K512/W16/R1 float below; both twins switched together so chunked-vs-tokenwise byte identity holds by construction and was verified byte-exact (513x3/2052/2049 + 368 bench identity checks). Measured with matched binaries: pair F32 family 6530.9 -> 995.9 ms per 2048 tokens (6.56x, mandate 2.5x), pair probe 89.15 -> 116.76 tok/s, slice 842.1 -> 1083.6 tok/s (target >=1050), decode guard 16.59 -> 15.91 ms/token. All gates PASS on the final tree: executor oracle 7.481e-07 vs 2e-4 cap (double was 7.484e-07; per-projection float delta <= 5.9e-08 rel_rms, no cap re-derivation needed), mhc/kda/dsa/batch_select ops tests, byte-equality trio, pair TP cross-rank oracle 0.000000, check-format 557 files; indexer top-k selection arithmetic verified untouched and still double. Production was parked only for the pair A/B window and restored (active, /ready=200 on 9th poll).
+- Phase 5 (Pair: chunk-width re-sweep + exchange accounting): Fix round 2: both reviewers found glm53_pair.py's DEFAULT_BINARY still pointing at the serving-campaign package (09c105f, kMaxBatch=2048), which would silently clamp the new --chunk 4096 default to 2048 while the state file recorded 4096 and the measurement assert was only <=. Fixed structurally: built a fresh tp2-tbstream package from the phase-5 tree (nix build .#tp2-tbstream at 42f9518 → /nix/store/j63y3jh685cp8krwyz1qf7yv39nhwx5d-gufo-0-unstable-42f9518, bin/gufo sha256 8d882f06…, nix hash sha256:02adk1lj…), shipped it to host B via nix-store --export | ssh … --import, and hash-verified it identical on both hosts; DEFAULT_BINARY now points there with a comment on the kMaxBatch coupling. Fixed defensively: glm53_serving_prefill.py now asserts max_prefill_chunk_tokens == min(fresh, chunk) (cold chunks ceil-split) with a diagnostic naming the silent stale-binary clamp — verified by simulation that a clamped 2048 serving width fails while correct single- and multi-chunk shapes pass; glm53_pair.py start records the launched binary's binary_sha256 in the state next to the requested chunk; --pair-state errors are clean messages (missing file / missing key both verified). README documents the ship-the-store-path step, the default-binary coupling warning, and the equality assertion. Checks re-run: py_compile both harnesses, check-docs PASS (75 files), nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.pr rc 0 (includes check-pr-tests); no C++ changed. Committed b0b439a; production active, /ready 200.
+- Phase 6 (Package + serving qualification): Re-ran the full package-identity verification live from this ssh-capable environment at 2026-10-11T06:49:06Z and appended the dated block to /tmp/opencode/p6v/logs/binary-identity.log: B's nix-store -q --hash = sha256:06h5b9r22czmw8694hw8m783i0i0ngxsqmlx3v01w1bycpkz3ffx and B's bin/gufo sha256 = 76075839e5e34557b384fd8a1df42e7faa782ca4d18760b0a76f5e678ae11db8, both equal to A's recomputed values, plus a fresh ssh-streamed full byte-compare (cmp rc=0) — the log now carries two independent matching blocks. Fixed the two accuracy items the review evidence surfaced: docs/models/glm-5.3-flash/README.md now states the harness's real assertion (cached_tokens < 200, measured 0 on every qualifying run, server log independently cache=miss cached_tokens=0) instead of overstating 'asserting cached_tokens = 0', and glm53_serving_prefill.py records prompt_tokens and cached_tokens in each report.json run entry so the cold evidence is self-contained in future artifacts (entry-dict shape sanity-checked; past reports keep their evidence in the printed lines, serve-6w-cold-evidence.tsv and the rank-0 log, all unchanged). Added a fix-round section to notes/serving-ws-250.md documenting the re-proof and both fixes. py_compile on both harnesses PASS, tools/ci/check-docs.py PASS (76 files); no C++ changed so check-format carries. Committed b306c8e on top of bfa5a3c; production untouched and verified active with /ready 200.
+- Phase 7 (Residual iteration + final verify/docs): Fix round 1: corrected the roofline-table arithmetic error the reviewer's recompute exposed — the note's 'everything else' row was ≈3544/10.8%/0.87 instead of the true 1173.6 ms / 3.6% / 0.29 ms/token — and root-caused it: the KDA recurrence kernel's register-column-rewrite name (BatchKdaRecurrenceRegKernel) matched no prof.py stage rule, so 486.3 ms hid in the census's 'other' bucket while the table's KDA row counted it explicitly. Fixed prof.py's glm stage map (both Reg names added; verified on the unchanged pair4096 DB — kda: recurrence 486.28 ms now attributes, other drops to 3.10 ms; corrected census archived in p7v), corrected the serial-stack aggregate to 1.15 ms/token (13.2% of wall) and the floor cross-check to 5.28 ms/token ≈ 189 tok/s in notes/final-ws-250.md, HANDOVER-TBSTREAM.md and the strix-dual-exp plan doc (committed there). For criterion-3 verifiability, re-ran all four checks live at 2026-10-11T07:58:21Z — HANDOVER phase-7 close section (115.0 tok/s, campaign trajectory, package de3a1f8) present; plan doc 'closed 2026-10-11 at 115.0 / NOT MET on a measured roofline' + evidence/glm53-flash/p7v/ with 20 items; gufo-prod active and /ready 200; worktree clean — logged to criterion3-reverify.log, copied into p7v, and documented in the note's new fix-round section. The reviewers' two environmental notes (ctest '^glm5_next_' regex matching nothing; glm5_next.reference glibc-2.42/2.43 loader skew, PASS with LD_LIBRARY_PATH) needed no tree change and are recorded as environment-only. check-docs PASS (77 files), prof.py byte-compiles, worktree committed clean at 84e53a2.
