+# GLM-5.3-Flash TP2 prefill 250 tok/s — phase 2 (vllm goal): expert
+# grouped-GEMM weight-stationary rewrite (2026-10-11)
+
+Target: `BatchExpertGroupedKernel` (+ routing helpers/launcher), the MoE
+family the phase brief puts at 31% of pair kernel time with a 3479 ms →
+≤900 ms mandate (a 3.86× cut). All prototype numbers: `tools/bench/
+expert_ws_bench.hip` (standalone HIP via `tools/bench/build.sh`), realistic
+top-8-of-288 routing (uniform + Zipf-0.6 skew; 2048-token sample: mean
+bucket 56.9, p50 57/p90 67/max 83 uniform and p50 39/p90 94/max 636 skewed;
+per-1024-token chunk the mean bucket is 28.4), real Q4_K block layout, the
+four production shapes (gate/up m1024 k4096 xs4096 and down m4096 k1024 xs1
+at TP2; m2048/m4096 k4096/2048 at TP1). Integrated numbers: `gpu-test`
+build, model `/root/models/glm53-flash/GLM-5.3-Flash-Q4_K_XL-00001-of-00005.gguf`.
+
+**Unit note (reviewer-requested):** the 3479 ms figure is
+notes/final-250.md's table row "expert Q4_K grouped … measured time" per
+**1024-token chunk per rank** (mean bucket 28.4 = the 1024-wide chunk
+occupancy); the phase brief's "per 2048 tokens" phrasing would double it to
+~6958 ms. Either way the commanded 3.86× cut is the target; this phase
+measures and lands what the hardware allows and documents the ceiling.
+
+## What actually bounds the family (measured, not modeled)
+
+The prototype swept three structural families against a verbatim copy of
+the landed kernel (V0):
+
+1. **A-family — bucket-resident accumulators.** `sums[Rows][B]` live in
+   registers across the whole K stream (compile-time chunk indices — the
+   first attempt indexed `sums[r][chunk+t]` at runtime and spilled to scratch,
+   costing 1.5-2×), each weight sub-block is decoded once per (row, K-tile)
+   and reused by every StageB-wide staging chunk, one butterfly per
+   (row, pair) exactly like V0 → **bit-identical to V0 by construction**
+   (verified max|diff| = 0 at every batched shape/width, plus the equality
+   harness below).
+2. **Y-family — slab block** (one block owns 512-1024 rows of the expert,
+   x staged once per K-tile and reused by all row groups, per-tile
+   butterflies flushed into y with a read-modify-write accumulate).
+   **Rejected on measurement**: 49.5-53.5 ms vs V0's 23.8 at gateTP2/1024
+   tokens — the per-(row, chunk, tile) butterflies and lane-0 global RMW
+   serialize far worse than the 8× x-staging saving pays.
+3. **Compile-time specialization** (template on Sub16/Vec): drops the Q8_0
+   branch (wqf[32]) and the scalar staging path from the hot Q4_K
+   instantiation — 106 → 82-87 VGPRs. This, not the loop restructure, is
+   where the measurable wins come from.
+
+The decisive measurements (uniform routing, TP2 shapes, BEST of 5):
+
+| Variant (B, StageB, Warps, Rows) | VGPR / waves | LDS | gate@512/1024/2048 ms | down@512/1024/2048 ms | n=1 gate/down ms | bit-identity |
+| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| V0 16/512/16/2 (landed) | 106 / 12 | 34.9 KiB | 12.75 / 24.18 / 47.79 | 15.88 / 29.50 / 57.23 | 0.139 / 0.311 | reference |
+| S16-W16R2 (V0 shape specialized) | 85 / 12 | 34.9 KiB | 12.65 / 23.95 / 47.19 | 15.24 / 28.87 / 55.94 | 0.123 / 0.214 | ok |
+| S32-W16R2 | 119 / 12 | 34.9 KiB | 13.19 / 25.01 / 49.17 | 16.96 / 31.59 / 59.88 | 0.149 / 0.348 | ok |
+| S32-W32R2 (rpb 64, x/2) | 117 / 12 | 34.9 KiB | 15.82 / 29.15 / 56.24 | 20.29 / 36.28 / 69.58 | 0.178 / 0.397 | ok |
+| S32-W16R1 (rpb 16, x×2) | 82 / 12 | 34.9 KiB | 13.34 / 25.83 / 50.89 | 16.85 / 32.01 / 61.34 | 0.171 / 0.362 | ok |
+| **S32-W32R1 (prefill winner)** | **82 / 16** | 34.9 KiB | **12.18 / 23.70 / 47.56** | **14.83 / 28.07 / 55.90** | 0.147 / 0.330 | ok |
+| S48-W16R1 / S48-W32R1 | 100 / 12 | 34.9 KiB | 13.45 / 16.94 | 17.41 / 21.37 | 0.217 / 0.556 | ok |
+| S64-W32R1 / S64-W32R2 | 119 / 9, 191 / 8 | 34.9 KiB | 13.65-17.66 | 18.29-25.70 | 0.222 / 0.550 | ok |
+| S16-W32R4 / S32-W32R4 (rpb 128, x/4) | 118-185 / 8 (+ spills) | 34.9 KiB | 15.32 / 29.19 | 19.22 / 36.32 | 0.185 / 0.339 | ok |
+| S16S8-W16R2 (decode winner) | 87 / 16 | 17.5 KiB | 12.87 / 25.11 / 49.97 | 15.74 / 29.63 / 57.46 | **0.097 / 0.196** | ok |
+| S16S4-W16R2 | 96 / 16 | 8.7 KiB | 15.37 / 29.74 | 18.70 / 35.73 | **0.089 / 0.190** | ok |
+| S32S8/S32S4/W8 shapes | 123-256 / 5-10 | 8.7-17.5 KiB | 17.09-64.48 | 22.08-152 | 0.162-0.875 | ok |
+| Y16 slab 1024 (rejected) | — | 34.9 KiB | 27.41 / 53.54 / 108.59 | 26.67 / 51.98 / 105.28 | 0.781 / 0.285 | n/a (RMW) |
+
+Skewed routing (Zipf 0.6) shifts every row by ≤2% — the plateau is not a
+routing-distribution artifact.
+
+### The measured blocking ceiling (why 3.86× is unreachable here)
+
+- **The family is register/occupancy-bound, not weight-DRAM-bound.**
+  Same-traffic pairs that differ only in VGPR count separate by 40%
+  (S48-W32R1, 100 VGPR/12 waves, 16.94 ms vs S32-W32R1, 82/16, 12.18);
+  doubling the x-restaging mandate (S32-W16R1, rpb 16) costs only +9%;
+  halving it (S32-W32R2, rpb 64, 117 VGPR) is +24% *slower*. Traffic
+  models that ignore occupancy predict the opposite of every measurement.
+- **The x-restaging term dominates the mandate and is register-capped.**
+  Per call it is (m/rpb) × pairs × k × 4 B = 4.3 GB at 1024-wide TP2 gate
+  vs 0.68 GB of weights-once. Its only lever is rows-per-block =
+  Warps×Rows, but `sums[Rows][B]` must stay ≤ ~128 registers: rpb 64 needs
+  117-142 VGPRs (slower), rpb 128 spills (185 VGPRs + spill stores, ~2×
+  slower). gfx1151's 256-VGPR ceiling and the 64 KiB LDS cap (StageB×512
+  staging tile; 16 pairs at 512 K = 34.9 KiB = 1 block per LDS unit) close
+  the space.
+- **Smaller LDS does not unlock prefill**: StageB 8/4 variants (17.5/8.7
+  KiB, 3-7 blocks per unit) measure 12.87-31.37 ms — the extra staging
+  passes and barriers cost more than the residency returns (they do win
+  25-40% at n=1, which is why one is the decode shape).
+- **The bit-identity twin constraint is not the binding wall**: the only
+  structure it forbids (per-tile butterflies enabling slab blocks / LDS
+  accumulators) was built and measured 2× slower (Y-family) — relaxing the
+  contract would not pay on this silicon.
+
+Within {256 VGPR, 64 KiB LDS, twin bit-identity} the plateau is V0 ±4%;
+the commanded 3479 → ≤900 ms (3.86×) is therefore **not achievable by tile
+restructuring on gfx1151**. The residual family time is x-restaging and
+weight bytes already near the ~240 GB/s mixed-stream ceiling at the mandate
+the register file permits. Next levers live outside this family: the Q8/F32
+dense tiles (57% of slice kernel time), the serial term (2.27 ms/token),
+or an executor-level restructure (e.g. gate+up fusion doubling the shared
+x audience) — phase 3+ territory.
+
+## Winner (landed)
+
+`BatchExpertGroupedWsKernel<Bucket, StageB, Warps, Rows>` in
+`kernels_batch.hip.cpp` — the A-family template, Sub16 + vector staging
+only, dispatched by `BatchExpertQ8KGrouped` (kernel changes confined to the
+kernel, its launcher and the prof.py stage map; executor untouched):
+
+- **Prefill (n ≥ 64): `<32, 16, 32, 1>`** — 82 VGPRs/16 waves, weight
+  passes ⌈bucket/32⌉ (≈1.13× at 1024-wide chunks vs the generic tile's
+  ≈2×), gate 12.18 vs 12.75 / down 14.83 vs 15.88 ms (−4.5/−6.7% at 512
+  tokens, −2/−4% at 1024-2048).
+- **Decode/small batch (n < 64, mean bucket < 2): `<16, 8, 16, 2>`** —
