+### Harness correction (retracted claim)
+
+An earlier run suggested V0's chunked path diverged from its tokenwise path
+at the TP2 gate shape (m=1024, k=4096, xs=4096, N ≤ 384). That was **a
+bench artifact, not a kernel defect**: the tokenwise loop routed each token
+in isolation, so `ExpertScatterKernel` wrote *local* pair indices 0..7
+(every token computed against token 0's activations, y writes collapsed
+into y[0..8m)), and each finalist after the first reused the stale
+single-token routing for its "chunked" run — producing exactly the observed
+first-shape-only asymmetry. After fixing both (a token scatter carrying
+global pair indices; full-N routing re-run before every chunked launch),
+**V0 and all variants are chunked-vs-tokenwise identical everywhere**
