+486.3 ms, other 3.1 ms) is archived in
+`/tmp/opencode/p7ws/logs/pair4096-census-fixed.txt` and
+`evidence/glm53-flash/p7v/pair4096-census.txt`.)
+
+## Ranked residual bottlenecks (final, quantified)
+
+1. **Expert Q4_K grouped — 3.19 ms/token (36.7 % of the 8.69 wall).** The
+   single largest block, unchanged by this campaign's retiles: phase 2
+   measured the family register/occupancy-bound (same-traffic VGPR pairs
+   separate 40 %; every rpb/row-raising tile spills or loses occupancy);
+   the 3.86× cut to its weights-once roofline share (0.82 ms/token) is
+   unreachable within {256 VGPR, 64 KiB LDS, byte identity}. Further gain
+   needs a different execution model — persistent expert residency or INT4
+   matrix-core paths — the former a redesign, the latter a numerics change
+   outside this goal's relaxation scope.
+2. **Q8_0 quant tiled — 2.07 ms/token (23.8 %).** Phase 3: streams its
+   actual 1018 GB/chunk traffic at ~99 % of the mixed ceiling; the
+   weights-once+x floor is 1.02 ms/token. The residual lever is cutting
+   the x-restaging *volume* (data layout/contract question), not the tile.
+3. **Serial stack (norm + KDA + HC + absorb + everything else outside the
+   five named families) — ≈ 1.15 ms/token (13.2 % of the 8.69 wall).**
+   The phase-1 serial term (2.27 ms/token including the MLA
+   gathers, which the split addressed) is architecture-shaped: vLLM's own
+   fixed cost at the same call site is 2.25 ms/token. KDA prepare/scan
+   parallelism is the known remaining lever (~0.35 ms/token).
+4. **Sparse MLA (split) — 0.72 ms/token.** Down from 1.09. The score half
+   (0.53) is fp32 dot + double-exp throughput; the next structural lever
+   is a float-exp softmax — a numerics relaxation needing the phase-4
+   evidence chain (measured binding-constraint proof, both twins switched,
+   re-derived caps, reviewer signoff), not taken unattended. The gather
+   half (0.19) broadcasts probs across threads — LDS staging is the
+   identified follow-up if it ever matters.
+5. **Indexer scores — 0.53 ms/token.** Double-precision top-k selection is
+   a stated contract; vLLM's fp16-WMMA indexer (their §42, 8.7–8.9×) is
+   contract-incompatible. Legal lever: double-precision batching/tiling.
+6. **F32 tiled — 0.34 ms/token.** Done (phase 4, 6.56×).
+7. **Wire/serving layer — ≈ 0.70 ms/token** (wall − kernel sum; write
+   9.4 % of prefill wall at 0.625 ms/MiB, wait ≤ 0.2 %, serving-vs-probe
+   ≈ +2 %). Becomes relevant only after another ~2× stage cut.
+
+Floor cross-check: expert at its roofline share (0.82) + Q8 at its
+weights-once+x floor (1.02) + everything else as measured today
+(0.72 + 0.53 + 1.15 + 0.34 + 0.70 wire) ≈ **5.28 ms/token ≈ 189 tok/s** —
+i.e. 250 tok/s at this depth is not reachable even with both mover
+families at their proven floors unless the expert/Q8 execution models or
+the serial/indexer contracts also move. That is the honest close.
+
+## vLLM same-depth comparison (their claim: 278–294 tok/s, 5.8K–19.9K)
+
+| depth | gufo (this tree) | gufo (phase-6 tree) | vLLM band | gap |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| ~3.4K | **115.0** | 110.3 | — (their shallowest point is 5.8K) | — |
+| ~5.9K | **105.9** | 101.2 | 291–294 | 2.75× |
+| ~15.9K | **86.7** | 83.0 | ~278–285 | 3.2× |
+
+Methodology differences (both sides' numbers are per-request fresh-token
+prefill through HTTP with cold-prefix discipline — nonce/`cache_salt`
+prompts, `cached_tokens = 0` verified — and multi-run medians/best-of):
+their stack runs the AWQ W4A16 checkpoint (different quantization of the
+same weights; our oracle fixtures anchor Q4_K_XL), 8192-token prefill
+chunks (vs our qualified 4096), RCCL/TB collectives with a measured
+10–15 % prefill all-reduce share (our tbstream census: write 9.4 %
+overlapped, wait ≤ 0.2 %), and their MoE is 41.5 % of prefill GPU time at
+12–18 % of achievable FLOPS vs our expert family's 39.9 % at its register
+ceiling — the two stacks' profiles are dominated by the same family.
+Their fixed serial cost (2.25 ms/token, their §42 fit) equals ours
+(2.27 pre-campaign), evidence the KDA/DSA/HC serial stack is the
+architecture's floor on both engines. The ~2.7–3.2× gap therefore sits
+almost entirely in (1) their large-M expert GEMM path (weights-once by
+construction of the shape at 8192-wide chunks, ~227 rows/expert, running
+at 12–18 % FLOPS on Triton) vs our register-bound WS tiles, and (2) their
+fp16-WMMA indexer + FlashMLA-style attention kernels, which our contracts
+(indexer top-k double; chunked/tokenwise byte identity anchoring the CPU
