+# GLM-5.3-Flash TP2 prefill 250 tok/s — phase 6: package + serving qualification (2026-10-10)
+
+## Goal status: NOT MET — do not close the goal on this phase
+
+The goal objective ("iterate until at least 250 tok/s serving-level") is
+**not achieved** by this phase's result: the packaged, fully qualified
+candidate measures **75.0 tok/s** serving-level prefill (74.85–74.99 across
+3 runs; plus one 72.0 tok/s 5001-token point). The gap to 250 tok/s is
+**3.3×**. This phase is *qualification* — it packages the phase 2–5 tree,
+proves it end-to-end (18/18 driver, byte-identity gates, CPU suite, hashes on
+both hosts) and measures where the optimized tree actually serves today. The
+goal must remain open. What phase 7 owes, per this phase's measurements and
+phase 5's census attribution (stage/local compute = 93–95% of prefill wall;
+the wire is ~5%):
+
+1. tiled quant/F32 projections across **all** layers at full depth (the
+   slice-level phase 3 kernels are landed; the full-model pair remains
+   stage-bound),
+2. KDA serial-scan parallelism (chunked/blocked scan),
+3. MLA attention depth scaling beyond the phase-4 tiling.
+
+Serving-layer work is done: chunk width is a launch choice (`--prefill-chunk`,
+clamp mirrors `kMaxBatch` = 2048, 1024 is the qualified default) and the
+qualification scaffolding (`tests/functional/glm53_pair.py`,
+`tests/functional/glm53_serving_prefill.py`, the packaged store path) re-runs
+as-is for re-measurement after optimization.
+
+End-to-end qualification of the optimized tree: full in-worktree battery,
+packaged `tp2-tbstream` candidate shipped to both hosts, the 18-case API
+driver, and the serving-level prefill measurement on the two-host pair.
+
+Production was parked for the whole GPU/serving window (`systemctl stop
+gufo-prod`, 21:44:12 CEST, was active with `/ready` 200) and restored at phase
+end (`systemctl start gufo-prod`; `active`, `/ready` = **200** on the 4th poll
+after start, 22:04:45 CEST).
+
+## Serving-layer change: the prefill chunk clamp follows the engine bound
+
+Phase 5 chose **chunk 1024** but the GLM serving path still clamped every
+requested width to 512 (`kGlmMaxPrefillChunk = 512`,
+`src/cli/serve/inference_backend.cpp`), so the chosen width could not actually
+run through HTTP. One change, deferred to this phase by phase 5's notes:
+
+- `kGlmMaxPrefillChunk` now mirrors the engine's own batch bound
+  (`models::glm5_next::rocm::Executor::kMaxBatch` = 2048 after phase 5's
+  window/scratch widening), with the header include that makes `Executor`
+  visible to the CLI layer. A launch picks its width with `--prefill-chunk`;
+  the qualification below uses 1024 everywhere.
+- HTTP-level confirmation that the width runs: every >1024-token measured
+  request reports `usage.gufo.max_prefill_chunk_tokens = 1024` with
+  `prefill_chunks = ceil(tokens/1024)` (e.g. 3405 tokens → 4 chunks).
+
+No other functional source changes this phase.
+
+## Packaged candidate (both hosts, hashes verified)
+
+Built with `nix build .#tp2-tbstream` from the staged tree (goal branch +
+the clamp change; first build attempt failed on the missing `executor.hpp`
+include and was fixed before shipping):
+
+| Item | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| store path | `/nix/store/b5q9qjkx5zpzsf4x6jaxhszlbqvz0g4m-gufo-0-unstable-09c105f-dirty` |
