+# GLM-5.3-Flash TP2 prefill 250 tok/s — phase 3: QuantTiled + F32Tiled T-scaling (2026-10-10)
+
+Targets: `BatchQuantTiledKernel` (Q8_0/sub16 dense projections) and
+`BatchF32TiledKernel` — 56.2% + 12.7% of post-phase-2 slice kernel time
+(736 + ~166 ms per 512-token chunk).
+
+All numbers: `gpu-test` build, model
+`/root/models/glm53-flash/GLM-5.3-Flash-Q4_K_XL-00001-of-00005.gguf`,
+`--layers 4 --random-tokens <N> 1 --repeat 2` (BEST of two passes; noise
+~±1%). Slice = layers 0–2 KDA + layer 3 DSA/MoE.
+
+## Why the past T8 attempts regressed (the commanded question)
+
+Re-derived from the traffic/occupancy model and probed with
+`hipOccupancyMaxActiveBlocksPerMultiprocessor` on dummy kernels with the
+real LDS sizes (gfx1151: 64 KiB LDS per CU, >64 KiB impossible):
+
+| Shape | LDS | blocks/SM | warps/SM | defect |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| T4/K1024/W8 (phase-2 tree) | 16.5 KiB | 3 | 24 | baseline |
+| T8/K1024/W8 | 33 KiB | 1 | **8** | occupancy collapse — 1 block of 8 warps cannot hide DRAM latency |
+| T8/K512/W8 | 16.5 KiB | 3 | 24 | **half of every warp idles in the Q8_0 consumer**: one 32-element block per lane needs K ≥ 1024; at K=512 only 16 of 32 lanes hold a block |
+| T16/K512/W32 (winner) | 33 KiB | 1 | **32** | none — W scales with T |
+
+Fixes applied for the causes, not the symptoms: the block width rises
+with the token height (W32 = 32 warps/SM at 1 block), and the Q8_0
+consumer was restructured from "one 32-element block per lane" to
+**16-element runs** (the sub16 grid), which keeps all 32 lanes busy for
+any K that is a multiple of 512. Side effects: the block-row groups
+double (x-staging L2 traffic ∝ 1/(W·R)) and the per-lane reduction
+regrouping is covered by the CPU-oracle RMS cap (tokenwise and chunked
+share the kernel, so byte equality holds by construction).
+
+## Correctness war story: the 1-ulp slot-dependent contraction bug
+
+Mid-sweep the exec byte-equality gates (513/2052) failed with a
+deterministic 1-ulp divergence starting at token 15 (the last slot of
+the first full tile), at every chunk width and every T. Isolation work:
+
+- An exhaustive standalone A/B (`n=512` vs 512×`n=1` over every real
+  (m, k, type) including the y_stride q|k|v concatenation and the m=24
+  hc.fn tail) showed the kernels byte-identical — with random x the bug
+  does not reproduce.
+- In-executor relaunches with identical arguments reproduced the
+  batched value exactly (deterministic per binary), but any unrelated
+  codegen change (a dead `if (n == 0xFFFFFFFF)` statement, quad- vs
+  flat-grouped staging, extracting the consumer into a helper, even the
+  never-executed sub16 branch) flipped the failure on and off.
+
+Root cause: with the default `-ffp-contract=fast`, clang contracts
+floating-point expressions **per unrolled iteration**, and the loop-exit
+context makes the *last* unrolled token slot's contraction differ from
+slot 0's. A token's projection value therefore depends on which tile
+slot computes it — the tokenwise path (n=1) always uses slot 0, the
+chunked path uses the token's slot, so the two disagree in the last ulp
+exactly when the schedules differ. It is not a data race and not a
+miscompile of a single kernel; it is legal-but-slot-inconsistent
+contraction that the byte-equality contract forbids.
+
+**Fix: `-ffp-contract=on` for `kernels_batch.hip.cpp`** (statement-level
+contraction, uniform across iterations) plus wrapping-guard consumer
+loops (`if (t < tokens) { body }`, the BatchF32TiledKernel form) and
+live-row-only staging. Verified robust: three different dead-code
+perturbations of the final tree all keep exec-513 byte-identical; the
+pre-fix tree flipped on the first perturbation. The FP-contraction flag
+is set per source file in `src/models/glm5_next/CMakeLists.txt` with a
+comment; any future tiled kernel with unrolled token loops in this TU
+inherits the protection.
+
+## Variant sweep (512-token bench, tok/s; F32 held at 4/1024/8 unless noted)
+
+Baseline V0 = phase-2 tree (T4/K1024/W8/R1, one 32-block per lane).
+
+| Variant (T, K, W, R) | LDS | tok/s | vs V0 | note |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| V0 baseline | 16.5 KiB | 390.6 | — | gates PASS (phase-2 tree) |
+| restructure control A0: 4, 1024, 8, 1 | 16.5 KiB | 459.9 | +17.7% | run-split consumer + float4 staging + live-row skip, same shape |
+| A1: 8, 1024, 16, 1 | 33 KiB | 566.0 | +45.0% | weight re-reads /2 |
+| A4: 8, 512, 16, 1 | 16.5 KiB | 581.7 | +49.0% | |
+| A2: 16, 512, 16, 1 | 33 KiB | 591.2 | +51.4% | weight re-reads /4 |
+| A3: 16, 512, 32, 1 | 33 KiB | 594.0 | +52.1% | |
+| A5: 16, 512, 16, 2 | 33 KiB | 598.7 | +53.3% | 32 rows/block |
+| **A9: 16, 512, 32, 2 (WINNER)** | 33 KiB | **604.6** | **+54.8%** | 64 rows/block, 32 warps/SM |
+| A8: 16, 512, 8, 1 | 33 KiB | 482.4 | +23.5% | W8 starves at 1 block/SM |
+| A6: 8, 1024, 16, 2 | 33 KiB | 533.5 | +36.6% | K1024 staging costs |
+| A10: 16, 512, 16, 4 | 33 KiB | 571.7 | +46.4% | register pressure |
+| A11: 16, 512, 32, 4 | 33 KiB | 553.6 | +41.8% | spills (sums[4][16]) |
+| A12: 16, 512, 32, 3 | 33 KiB | 567.1 | +45.2% | spills |
+| A13: 16, 512, 24, 2 | 33 KiB | 603.0 | +54.4% | ties winner |
+| P1: winner + pipelined staging | 33 KiB | 562.1 | +44.0% | REJECTED (below) |
+
+T32 is infeasible: K512 staging would need 66 KiB LDS (> 64 KiB cap) and
+K256 idles half the run grid (16 runs < 32 lanes). The final tree runs
+the winner with the contraction-safe consumer and float4 quad staging,
+measuring 606.3–609.0 across three runs — the uniform-contraction fix
+cost nothing measurable (604.6 pre-fix) and the sweep ordering stands.
+
+### Pipelined staging (LDS double-buffering axis) — rejected
+
+gfx1151 has no async global→LDS copy, so double buffering degenerates to
+a register-mediated pipeline (load tile i+1 into registers during tile
+i's compute, commit between barriers; the LDS budget also forbids two
+33 KiB buffers). Measured 604.6 → 562.1 at the winner shape: the
+compiler sinks the prefetch loads to their commit point, so the extra
+barrier and register pressure buy nothing. Removed.
+
+## F32 family sweep (quant fixed at 16/512/32/R2)
+
+| Variant (T, K, W, R) | tok/s |
+| --- | ---: |
+| F0 control 4, 1024, 8, 1 | 604.6 |
+| F1: 8, 1024, 16, 1 | 607.5 |
+| F2: 16, 512, 16, 1 | 610.4 |
+| F3: 8, 1024, 8, 1 | 606.3 |
+| F4: 16, 1024, 16, 1 | 605.0 |
+| **F5: 8, 512, 16, 1 (CHOSEN)** | 609–611.1 |
+| F6: 16, 512, 32, 1 | 608.1 |
+| F7: 8, 512, 32, 1 | 606.7–611.7 |
+| F8: 8, 512, 16, 2 | 608.9 |
+
+The whole family moves ≤ 6 tok/s: at ~25.6 G double FMAs per chunk the
+kernel is FP64-throughput-bound (gfx1151 FP64 ≈ 1/64 rate), so T-scaling
+only trims the weight re-reads (166 → 157.6 ms/chunk measured, −5%).
+F5 chosen (mid-shape, clean LDS at 16 KiB = 4 blocks/SM). R2 does not
+pay (F8) — the x-staging term is small next to the FP64 floor.
+
+## Winner (landed)
+
+`kQuantTokens=16, kQuantK=512, kQuantWarps=32, kQuantRows=2` —
+`kF32Tokens=8, kF32K=512, kF32Warps=16, kF32Rows=1` — plus:
+
+- Q8_0 consumer on 16-element runs (full warp at any K ≥ 512 multiple),
+  int8→float hoisted per run;
+- float4 global staging reads (quad-grouped, scalar fallback for odd k),
+  live rows only — decode stages one row regardless of tile height;
+- `-ffp-contract=on` on the TU (the slot-uniformity fix above);
+- launcher reroutes `m % (warps·rows) != 0` (e.g. a 24-row hc.fn-shaped
+  quant tensor in other artifacts) to the wave GEMV so the tiled kernel's
+  staging/barrier collective always gets whole row groups.
+
+### Numerics decision (recorded per phase contract)
+
+- The K/T/W regroupings change per-lane partial shapes only; tokenwise
+  and chunked dispatch the identical kernel, so chunk-vs-tokenwise byte
+  equality is by construction and passed on the final tree (max|diff| =
+  0 at 513 and 2052 tokens, logits + persistent state).
+- CPU-oracle 5-token logits rel_rms **7.484e-07** (cap 2e-4; phase-2
+  value 7.576e-07 — the shift is the run-split + contraction=on
+  rounding, two orders of magnitude inside the cap).
+- The contraction flag makes FP rounding slot-uniform; it does not
+  introduce fast-math (no reassociation, no denormal flushing).
+
+## Before/after (same binaries protocol, phase-start vs final tree)
+
+| Measurement | before | after | Δ |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Slice 512-token bench | 390.6 tok/s | 606.3–609.0 tok/s | **+55.4%** |
