+**Related prefill rounds worth mining (PATCHES.md):**
+
+- **§8 (GLM chunk size)**: 512 → 2048/4096-token chunks took prefill
+  151 → 189–206 tok/s; returns flatten after 2048. The old 512 cap was
+  superstition (the indexer workspace does not scale with the knob). Their
+  remaining per-chunk cost was ~87 latency-bound all-reduces — a vLLM/RCCL
+  artifact we do not share (see REJECTED).
+- **§42 (DS4 prefill)**: at 512-token chunks "the prefill MoE is
+  weight-bound: each chunk reads every expert" — moving to **2048-token
+  chunks** (plus an indexer kernel and mHC tiles) took DS4 8 K prefill
+  23.1 s → 14.9 s (~460 tok/s) and left a fixed cost of **2.25 ms/token**
+  (fit T(L) = 2.25 ms·L + 1.2e-8·L²/2). That fixed per-token cost on their
+  stack is strikingly equal to our measured serial term (2.27 ms/token):
+  the KDA/DSA/hyper-connection serial stack costs ~2.25–2.27 ms/token on
+  *both* engines — it is the architecture's floor, not a gufo defect.
+- **§6 (MoE tile configs)**: stock `BLOCK_SIZE_K=32` loaded only 16 packed
+  bytes per row per K-step → 38 GB/s; tuned JSON tiles (BLOCK 32/32/128,
+  SPLIT_K 4 at M=1 … 16/32/64 above) fixed decode 1.6×. Calibration gold
+  nugget: their dense BF16 projections via `wvSplitK` move **4.7 GB in
+  ~22 ms = ~214 GB/s** on this GPU — proof that a well-shaped linear kernel
+  streams weights at ~89 % of the pure-read ceiling.
+- **§28.5 (`vsh_moe_int4.hip`)**: decode-sized int4 MoE GEMV, wvSplitK
+  style — activations staged once in LDS, 16 contiguous packed bytes per
+  lane per step, fp32 accumulate, cross-lane shuffle reduce; ≤ 64
+  (token, expert) pairs per block. Unit-measured 160–208 GB/s vs Triton's
+  70–80. The *structure* (LDS-stage x once, stream weights wide) is the
+  portable part; the ≤ 64-pair decode sizing is not.
+- **`vsh-w8a16-linear.py`**: BF16 linears re-quantized to int8 group-128 at
+  load; **≤ 8 rows run a HIP GEMV, larger batches dequantize once and run a
+  stock GEMM (hipBLASLt)** — at prefill M their linears are plain large-M
+  GEMMs, i.e. weights-once by construction of the shape.
+
+**Methodology (vsh_bench.py / vsh_ab.py):** per-request TTFT with streaming;
+prefill tok/s = prompt_tokens / TTFT; **cold-prefix discipline** = nonce
+(`cache_salt`-equivalent) baked into every prompt so the 2304-token
+prefix-cache blocks never hit, verified via `usage` cached_tokens = 0 and
+/metrics prefix-cache counters; medians of ≥ 2 boots or ≥ 5 repetitions;
+engine warmed first (first call at a new chunk shape pays Triton JIT and is
+explicitly excluded); `vsh_ab.py` counts steps engine-side (draft counters),
+never from HTTP chunk rates. Our equivalents: calibrated cold prefixes +
+3 runs + server-side usage (`tests/functional/glm53_serving_prefill.py`),
+probe-vs-server tracked at ~5 % (89.2 → 84.4 in the last campaign).
